    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d570">

                <pb facs="0677" n="1511" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1511"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/610</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Netherland Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">De
                            Beaufort</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 10, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: This Legation has
                    received the request from your Department to facilitate the shipment of five
                    barrels of flour, one case of ham, one case of bacon, one case of lard, and one
                    box from your Department to the United States Minister at The Hague. I have at
                    once cabled about this matter to the Minister of Foreign Affairs, and am today
                    informed that the Netherland Government makes no objection to allow this
                    shipment to go forward on a Netherland vessel and consigned to the Netherland
                    Government. Where repeated large shipments of food for the United States
                    Legation and consular officers prove that the United States authorities are
                    convinced that food is exceedingly scarce in Holland, the Netherland Government
                    trusts that the shipments of food for the Dutch people will be expedited.</p>
                <p>While informing you of the above I remain [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. de Beaufort</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
